            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "StacyB1012"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing!! I was afraid the jalapenos would be too much so I substituted a poblano pepper. So so good and even better the next day and the day after.",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-04T17:05:50.617Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gina Uebel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did not have the cilantro on hand and did without. I also had yellow onion instead of red. The fresh lime juice makes a huge difference. I will try it again with all the ingredients and some tomatoes from my garden.",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-22T10:04:23.127Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "myhomischi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent and easy. It was a big hit at the party. Ironically, the store must have had a run on jalapeños as they were out. I substituted 1 fresco instead (they are a little hotter). Definite, must make again.",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-06T09:46:19.273Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "swag35"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy!!! I made this with cilantro lime rice, also from this site, and used it in burritoes. It is also a great with tortilla chips. I don't like green peppers, so I used a sweet orange pepper. Also, I didn't have any jalepeno on hand, so I substituted a pablano pepper. Very tasty. When I open a can of chipotle in adobo, I blend it and keep in in the fridge or freeze in small amounts. I suggest adding a little at a time to reach your desired heat level. Next I will try this on fish tacos!",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-02T06:54:58.173Z"
          }
        ],
